@bjbartelt not so worried about them at the moment but there are so many new fiber providers including the old telcos like $T $TMUS $VZ  .  They are building fiber on top of fixed wireless (which is already eroding biz from $CHTR  and $CMCSA ) . 

Not to mention other smaller local overbuilders. It’s just a crowded space now. Not like the early days. A crowded trade you could say.

And $CHTR  is leveraged to the hilt and have made bad biz decisions for years. A culture changes very slowly if ever. You don’t hire nick jeffries if your future looks bright. 2 year turnaround min. And stock price will play catch up.
